{"id":"negatives","n":31,"unit":7,"title":"Saying no","goal":"Make negatives without doubling or mixing forms","wm":"Negative Sentences","intro":"To make a sentence negative, add “not” after the helping verb: isn’t, don’t, didn’t, haven’t, can’t, won’t. If there’s no helping verb, add do/does/did. Use only one negative word in a sentence: “I don’t know anything”, not “I don’t know nothing”.","rules":[{"rule":"helping verb + not.","examples":["She isn’t here.","We haven’t decided."]},{"rule":"don’t / doesn’t / didn’t + base form.","examples":["He doesn’t smoke.","I didn’t see it."]},{"rule":"One negative per sentence. Use any / anything / anyone after a negative.","examples":["I didn’t tell anyone.","There isn’t anything to eat."]}],"mistakes":[{"wrong":"I don’t know nothing.","right":"I don’t know anything.","why":"Only one negative."},{"wrong":"He not coming today.","right":"He isn’t coming today.","why":"Add the helping verb: isn’t."},{"wrong":"She didn’t called me.","right":"She didn’t call me.","why":"didn’t + base form"},{"wrong":"No, I didn’t went.","right":"No, I didn’t go.","why":"didn’t + base form"}],"ex":[{"k":"pick","q":"We ___ any milk left.","o":["don’t have","haven’t","not have"],"a":0,"y":"don’t + have"},{"k":"pick","q":"He ___ answer my call yesterday.","o":["didn’t","doesn’t","not"],"a":0,"y":"Past: didn’t."},{"k":"pick","q":"I didn’t say ___.","o":["nothing","anything","something"],"a":1,"y":"After a negative: anything."},{"k":"pick","q":"She ___ at home right now.","o":["not","isn’t","doesn’t"],"a":1,"y":"be + not: isn’t."},{"k":"spot","q":"My phone not charging properly.","w":"not charging","r":"isn't charging","at":9,"fixed":"My phone isn't charging properly.","y":"Add the helping verb."},{"k":"spot","q":"We didn't see nobody there.","w":"nobody","r":"anybody","at":14,"fixed":"We didn't see anybody there.","y":"One negative only."},{"k":"spot","q":"He doesn't wants to come.","w":"wants","r":"want","at":11,"fixed":"He doesn't want to come.","y":"doesn’t + base form"},{"k":"type","q":"I ___ (not / finish) the book yet.","a":["haven't finished","have not finished","haven’t finished"],"y":"Present perfect negative."},{"k":"order","a":"I didn't understand anything he said.","y":"didn’t + base form + anything"},{"k":"say","q":"Make it negative: “I told somebody.”","a":["I didn't tell anybody","I didn't tell anyone","I did not tell anybody","I did not tell anyone"],"y":"didn’t + tell + anyone"}],"talk":"Talk about three things you don’t like, two things you didn’t do last week, and one thing you have never done."}